<article class="env-proposition" id="04UA">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04UA">Proposition <span data-tag="04UA">10.2.1.12</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a morphism of simplicial sets. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The morphism $U$ restricts to an isomorphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ with a sieve $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{0} \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The morphism $U$ is a right covering map (Definition <a data-tag="022N" href="/tag/022N">4.2.3.8</a>) and, for every vertex $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the fiber $U^{-1} \{ C\} $ has at most one element. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      The implication $(1) \Rightarrow (2)$ follows from Example <a data-tag="022S" href="/tag/022S">4.2.3.12</a>. Conversely, suppose that condition $(2)$ is satisfied, and let $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ denote the homotopy category of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Our assumption that $U$ is a right covering map guarantees the existence of a pullback square 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\ar [r]^-{U} \ar [d] &amp;  \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \int ^{ \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} } \mathscr {F}) \ar [d] \\ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\ar [r] &amp;  \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} ) } \]
</div>
<p>
       where $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}^{\operatorname{op}} \rightarrow \operatorname{Set}$ is the contravariant homotopy transport representation of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, given concretely by the formula $\mathscr {F}(C) = U^{-1} \{ C\} $ (see Corollary <a data-tag="027X" href="/tag/027X">5.2.7.4</a>). Our assumption that each of the sets $\mathscr {F}(C)$ has at most one element guarantees that the right vertical map induces an isomorphism from $\int ^{ \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} } \mathscr {F}$ to the sieve $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\subseteq \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ spanned by those objects $C$ for which the fiber $U^{-1} \{ C\} $ is nonempty. Condition $(1)$ now follows from Example <a data-tag="04U6" href="/tag/04U6">10.2.1.7</a> and Remark <a data-tag="04U2" href="/tag/04U2">10.2.1.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
